  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Potential for frost tonight and Wednesday night\nacross the north.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure building into the area this morning may lead to\nfavorable radn/l cooling conditions as low lying valleys \ndecouple. Patchy/areas of frost are expected tonight and again \nWednesday night with temperatures dipping to near/below freezing\neach night in normally colder low lying and valley locations.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A coastal low could impact at least Downeast\nMaine late this week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nA coastal low is expected to develop across the Mid-Atlantic\nregion later this week while high pressure remains centered over\nQuebec. The track of the ocean low is still uncertain with \nblocking high pressure to the northwest of our forecast area and\nridging across the Great Lakes. Uncertainty remains regarding \nthe northern edge of the precipitation shield and whether rain \nwill reach Maine. Northerly to northeasterly winds could become \ngusty over the weekend, especially along the coast, as a tight \npressure gradient forms.",
